==German==

===Etymology===
Essentially, the term is a joke: in the local dialect, ''Kann isch ne halve han?'' means 'Can I get a half (of a sandwich)'; foreigners interpreted this as ''Halve Hahn'' ('half a rooster'). Nowadays, it's often written like this on the menus of rustical restaurants in Cologne.

===Noun===
'''Halve Hahn''' {{m}}

# {{context|Cologne dialect}} a [[cheese]] [[sandwich]], cut in half.

